11
00:54:36,428 --> 00:54:42,428
Fight Club is a 1999  American film directed by David Fincher and
starring Brad Pitt, Edward Norton, and Helena Bonham Carter.

12
00:59:34,285 --> 00:59:40,285
It is based on the 1996 novel by Chuck Palahniuk.

13
01:04:32,142 --> 01:04:38,142
Norton plays the unnamed narrator, who is
discontented with his white-collar job.

14
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:36,000
He forms a "fight club" with a soap salesman, Tyler Durden (Pitt), and becomes embroiled
with an impoverished but beguiling woman, Marla Singer (Bonham Carter).

15
01:14:27,857 --> 01:14:33,857
Palahniuk's novel was optioned by Fox 2000 Pictures producer Laura
Ziskin, who hired Jim Uhls to write the film adaptation.

16
01:19:25,714 --> 01:19:31,714
Fincher was selected because of his enthusiasm for the story.

17
01:24:23,571 --> 01:24:29,571
He developed the script with Uhls and sought screenwriting advice
from the cast and others in the film industry.

18
01:29:21,428 --> 01:29:27,428
It was filmed in and around Los Angeles from July to December 1998.

19
01:34:19,285 --> 01:34:25,285
He and the cast compared the film to Rebel Without a Cause (1955) and The Graduate (1967), with
a theme of conflict between Generation X and the value system of advertising.

20
01:39:17,142 --> 01:39:23,142
Studio executives did not like the film and restructured Fincher's
intended marketing campaign to try to reduce anticipated losses.

21
01:44:14,999 --> 01:44:20,999
Fight Club premiered at the 56th Venice International Film Festival on September 10, 1999, and
was released in the United States on October 15, 1999, by 20th Century Fox.

22
01:49:12,857 --> 01:49:18,857
The film failed to meet the studio's expectations at
the box office and polarized critics.

23
01:54:10,714 --> 01:54:16,714
It was ranked as one of the most controversial and
talked-about films of the 1990s.

24
01:59:08,571 --> 01:59:14,571
However, Fight Club later found commercial success with its home video release,
establishing it as a cult classic and causing media to revisit the film.

25
02:04:06,428 --> 02:04:12,428
In 2009, on its tenth anniversary, The New York Times dubbed
it the "defining cult movie of our time".

26
02:09:04,285 --> 02:09:10,285
The film explores themes of dual identity, rage and hate,
based on novel or book, nihilism, fight.

27
02:14:02,142 --> 02:14:08,142
The tone is emotional and intense.
